    "body": "### Problem\n\nPrinting into command line from inside mapping resets `[count]` with ui2 enabled via `{ msg = { targets = 'msg' } }` config.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create the following `init.lua`:\n\n    ```lua\n    require('vim._core.ui2').enable({ msg = { targets = 'msg' } })\n\n    _G.log = {}\n    vim.keymap.set('n', 'gm', function()\n      local count_init = vim.v.count\n      print('Hello')\n      table.insert(_G.log, { count_init = count_init, count_later = vim.v.count })\n    end)\n     ```\n\n2. `nvim --clean -u init.lua`\n3. `2gm`. Executing `:=log` shows `{ { count_init = 2, count_later = 0 } }`.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nPrinting into command line does not affect the `[count]` or any temporarily set variables that do not track command line printing.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1825+g402a494f47\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nNo\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nEndeavourOS Linux x86_64, 7.2.8-arch1-2\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nGhostty 1.3.1-arch2\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-ghostty\n\n### Installation\n\nAppimage",
